Subject: sbat: add a beast-booter vendor line

A modified build keeps the upstream "wimboot" SBAT line and adds its own
vendor line (SBAT.md, "product.vendor"), so the metadata describes the
code truthfully. beast-booter ships wimboot unsigned (Windows boots with
Secure Boot off), so the line is informational.

---
--- a/src/efimain.c
+++ b/src/efimain.c
@@ -44,6 +44,10 @@
 	/* wimboot version */						\
 	"wimboot," SBAT_GENERATION ",iPXE,wimboot," VERSION ","		\
 	"https://ipxe.org/wimboot"					\
+	"\n"								\
+	/* Modified build (see the vendor's patches) */			\
+	"wimboot.beastboot,1,BeastBoot,wimboot," VERSION ","		\
+	"https://github.com/cynak/BeastBoot"				\
 	"\n"
 
 /** SBAT metadata (with no terminating NUL) */
